fer that the tiger chases the lion.\n   - Since the tiger chases the lion and the lion sees the tiger, the tiger must see the lion.\n   - Therefore, the mouse does not see the lion because the tiger sees the lion and the mouse sees the tiger, but the mouse does not chase the lion.\n\nBased on this reasoning, the statement \"The mouse does not see the lion\" is true.\n\n<answer>\nA) True\n</answer>",
